---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Notice from '../components/Notice.astro';
import { project } from '../data/project.js';
import { recovery, topologies } from '../data/firmware.js';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const direct = topologies[0];
const dongle = topologies[1];
---
<SiteLayout title="Setup and troubleshooting" description="Flash, pair and troubleshoot Corney in Direct Bluetooth or USB Dongle mode, including OLED and trackpad behavior." current="guide">
  <div class="shell page-hero"><span class="eyebrow">Guide / from blank controllers to typing</span><h1>Get connected.<br />Stay connected.</h1><p class="lead">Follow the topology you chose on the firmware page. Keep all operating images from one release together and use settings reset only when you intend to clear stored bonds.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn" href={`${base}/firmware/`}>Choose firmware</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting ↓</a></div></div>
  <div class="shell guide-layout"><nav class="toc" aria-label="Guide sections"><span class="eyebrow">On this page</span><a href="#flash">Flash the controllers</a><a href="#direct">Pair Direct Bluetooth</a><a href="#dongle">Connect USB Dongle</a><a href="#switch">Switch topologies</a><a href="#oled">Read the OLED</a><a href="#pointing">Trackpad notes</a><a href="#troubleshooting">Troubleshooting</a></nav><div class="prose">
    <section id="flash"><span class="eyebrow">01 / install</span><h2>Flash the controllers</h2><ol><li>Choose <a href={`${base}/firmware/`}>Direct Bluetooth or USB Dongle</a> and identify the exact UF2 for each physical device.</li><li>Connect one {"nice!nano v2"} controller over USB. Put it in bootloader mode using its reset procedure, then copy its matching UF2 to the exposed bootloader drive.</li><li>Wait for the drive to disappear and the controller to restart. Repeat with the remaining half and, for dongle mode, the dedicated dongle.</li><li>Power both halves. In dongle mode, also connect the dongle to the host USB port.</li></ol><Notice title="Match the role before copying."><p>The left half is a central in Direct Bluetooth mode and a peripheral in USB Dongle mode. Their UF2 images are different; the right half uses the same <code>corney-right.uf2</code> image in both modes.</p></Notice></section>
    <section id="direct"><span class="eyebrow">02 / Direct Bluetooth</span><h2>Pair the left central</h2><p>Use <code>{direct.controllers[0].artifact}</code> on the left and <code>{direct.controllers[1].artifact}</code> on the right. Power both halves and allow the split link to connect. Pair the host with the <strong>Corney</strong> Bluetooth keyboard advertised by the left central.</p><p>The Functional layer contains ZMK Bluetooth clear and host-profile controls. See the <a href={project.docs.keymap}>current keymap</a> for their physical positions before changing bonds.</p></section>
    <section id="dongle"><span class="eyebrow">03 / USB Dongle</span><h2>Connect through USB</h2><p>Flash the dedicated dongle with <code>{dongle.controllers[0].artifact}</code>, the left half with <code>{dongle.controllers[1].artifact}</code> and the right half with <code>{dongle.controllers[2].artifact}</code>. Power both halves, then connect the dongle to the host over USB. Allow both split links to establish.</p><p>The dongle sends keyboard and pointer input as USB HID. Its separate BLE connection remains available to compatible Keyboard Helper clients.</p></section>
    <section id="switch"><span class="eyebrow">04 / changing the central</span><h2>Switch topologies carefully</h2><p>Changing which controller is central invalidates existing split bonds. To enter dongle mode, flash <code>{recovery.artifact}</code> on the future dongle and both halves, let each boot, then flash the three operating images listed above. To return to Direct Bluetooth, reset both halves and reset the dongle before its next use; then flash <code>{direct.controllers[0].artifact}</code> on the left and <code>{direct.controllers[1].artifact}</code> on the right. Pair the intended host again.</p><Notice title="Settings reset clears stored bonds." tone="warning"><p>The reset UF2 is temporary. Every controller that ran it needs its operating firmware restored before normal use.</p></Notice></section>
    <section id="oled"><span class="eyebrow">05 / dongle status</span><h2>Read the OLED</h2><p>The dongle's 128 × 64 OLED shows the output at upper left and local dongle battery at upper right. One row beneath the local battery contains two unlabeled remote percentages, such as <code>78% 56%</code>. The bottom row shows the full active layer name beside a keyboard symbol; long names scroll slowly instead of being truncated.</p><p><code>--</code> means a remote value is unavailable or disconnected. Pinned ZMK v0.3.0 also reports disconnect as zero, so a genuine remote <code>0%</code> appears as <code>--</code>. The pair follows split slot order and does not identify left or right. A local power symbol reports USB presence, not proof that a dongle cell is charging. The display blanks at idle and resumes with keyboard activity.</p><p>For electrical connections, use the <a href={`${base}/build/#oled`}>OLED wiring guide</a>.</p></section>
    <section id="pointing"><span class="eyebrow">06 / optional pointing</span><h2>Trackpad notes</h2><p>The same half firmware supports an optional Cirque sensor on either or both halves. A missing sensor does not stop the keys or the other half's installed sensor. Each installed sensor is polled while active; touch alone does not wake a sleeping controller without the data-ready connection. Press a key on that half to wake it, and allow the split link to reconnect if needed.</p><p>A simultaneous hold of the same mouse button from both sensors is unsupported. The dongle has no sensor of its own.</p></section>
    <section id="troubleshooting"><span class="eyebrow">07 / common questions</span><h2>When something does not respond</h2><div class="faq"><h3>Only one half types</h3><p>Confirm both halves are powered, that the right image is <code>corney-right.uf2</code>, and that the left image matches your topology. After changing central roles, clear old split bonds as described above.</p><h3>The host cannot find Corney</h3><p>In Direct Bluetooth mode, pair with the left central. In USB Dongle mode, connect the dongle by USB for keyboard input; BLE is a separate Keyboard Helper connection.</p><h3>The OLED shows <code>--</code></h3><p>Wait for both halves to connect and send battery readings. If one stays unavailable, check that half's power and split bond. The two fields cannot be assigned to physical sides from their positions.</p><h3>The trackpad stops after sleep</h3><p>Wake the sensor-equipped half with a key, then allow split reconnect. Trackpad contact alone is not a wake source in this wiring.</p><h3>I need deeper implementation evidence</h3><p>The <a href={project.docs.pointing}>trackpad verification</a>, <a href={project.docs.oled}>OLED verification</a>, and <a href={project.docs.protocol}>Keyboard Helper protocol</a> are contributor documents. Normal installation does not require them.</p></div></section>
  </div></div>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
.guide-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:220px minmax(0,1fr);gap:85px;align-items:start}.toc{position:sticky;top:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:22px;border-radius:9px}.toc .eyebrow{margin-bottom:5px}.toc a{color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;font-size:.87rem}.toc a:hover{color:var(--accent)}.prose section{scroll-margin-top:25px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:38px;margin-bottom:50px}.prose section:first-child{border-top:0;padding-top:0}.prose section>.eyebrow{display:block;margin-bottom:12px}.prose h2{margin-top:0;font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.3rem)}.prose h3{font-size:1.14rem;margin:28px 0 8px}.prose p{margin-bottom:15px}.faq{border-left:1px solid var(--border);padding-left:22px}.faq h3:first-child{margin-top:0}
@media(max-width:800px){.guide-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:40px}.toc{position:static;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.toc .eyebrow{grid-column:1/-1}}
@media(max-width:480px){.toc{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
